## Self-review

Reviewed all BUY/SELL call sites and confirmed V5 routes them through the centralized friction-aware
entry, scale-out, and close paths. Reviewed staged scope, schema branching, pending cancellation,
terminal liquidation, and checkpoint restore. No remaining Task 2 finding after the terminal-equity
journal fix.

## Review fix round

Addressed all four Important findings from `task-2-review.md` without modifying tests or widening
the source scope:

- V5 queued policy exits now require a valid exact-session `Open`; a prior-session price is never
  used for an open-phase fill, and the pending exit survives until an eligible open exists.
- V5 selected evictions now separately require the held symbol's valid exact-session `Open` at the
  fill boundary. Stale prices remain permitted only for non-fill valuation; a missing eviction open
  declines the projected transition and leaves the holding intact.
- Phase 5 now closes any still-open position whose causal stop resolver fires. Phase 2 has already
  removed pre-open gap-stop holdings, so a remaining `gap_stop` is precisely the same-session-entry
  case where adverse friction placed the actual-fill-derived stop above the reference open. The
  position map prevents double closes.
- Friction components are allocated in integer cents from their unrounded relative weights so their
  reported sum exactly equals the cash-delta friction boundary. `_record_v5_fill` independently
  enforces that reconciliation before emitting evidence.
- Restored legacy result compatibility by moving `fill_log` and `fill_cost_totals` into the
  `SimulationResultV5` subtype. Successful legacy runs return the original `SimulationResult`
  field/schema shape and do not initialize or expose V5 fill-cost totals. V5 live and resumed runs
  return the subtype required by later optimizer consumers.

