### Fix-round deterministic smoke — pass

The provider-free smoke used local OHLCV, a ten-symbol local RS cross-section, and an in-process
static strategy. Temporary script, checkpoint, progress, and state-journal files were removed after
the run. Its final evidence was:

```json
{"checkpoint_resume_type":"SimulationResultV5","legacy_result_fields":["benchmark_curve","benchmark_symbol","config","entry_outcomes","equity_curve","execution_diagnostics","initial_capital","signal_log","trades","transaction_log","weekly_holdings"],"missing_open_eviction_declined":true,"missing_open_pending_retained":1,"one_cent_friction":0.01,"same_session_stop":"stop_loss"}
```

The smoke asserted that a queued exit survived when only the prior bar existed; an eviction was
declined under the same missing-open condition; a high-bps same-session entry whose derived stop was
already crossed closed through phase 5; three sub-cent friction components reconciled to the one-cent
cash impact and V5 aggregate; a successful legacy result had neither V5 field in dataclass/asdict
serialization nor as attributes; and a completed schema-5 checkpoint resumed into
`SimulationResultV5` with identical fill evidence and totals.
